<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8"><div data-thread-user-message-navigation-content="true" style="width: calc(100% - 2 * var(--thread-wide-block-inline-shift)); margin-inline: auto;" class="relative flex flex-1 shrink-0 flex-col transcriptContent-l_FOQD [--thread-content-max-width:var(--thread-content-responsive-max-width,inherit)] [--thread-body-max-width:calc(var(--thread-content-max-width)+var(--thread-body-inline-padding,0px)*2)] mx-auto w-full max-w-(--thread-body-max-width) px-[var(--thread-body-inline-padding,var(--padding-toolbar))] pb-8 has-[[data-compact-status-slot-clearance]]:pb-0" data-mcp-app-portal-target="true"><div data-chatgpt-conversation-selection-target="local-chatgpt:ee0c06f9-24e3-4f15-93c2-579cafc84c9f" class="flex min-h-full flex-1 flex-col gap-1.5 pb-5" data-thread-find-target="conversation" style="transform: none;"><div class="relative shrink-0" style="height: 15282px;"><div class="flex flex-col" style="margin-top: 13064px;"><div class="" style="contain: size; height: 1658px; margin-top: 0px;"><div class="[&amp;_[data-virtualized-turn-content]]:[content-visibility:visible]" data-turn-key="9703fabe-414a-4e12-8a1b-ebf7cb8bcbeb"><div data-content-search-turn-key="fallback-turn-2"><div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5"><div class="group flex flex-col" data-talvt-turn-state="complete"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3 browser:gap-1"><div class="block-BQZwFn"><div class="group/user-message flex flex-col items-end gap-2" data-chatgpt-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-2:0:user" data-chatgpt-search-message-ids="9703fabe-414a-4e12-8a1b-ebf7cb8bcbeb"><div class="w-full" data-content-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-2:0:user"><div class="group/user-message flex w-full flex-col gap-1 print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:items-start items-end"><div data-user-message-bubble="true" class="bg-user-message text-user-message min-w-0 max-w-(--user-chat-width) overflow-hidden break-words px-(--thread-content-margin) [&amp;_.contain-inline-size]:[contain:initial] bubble-vBnidZ py-2.5 rounded-2xl relative text-start"><div class="flex flex-col items-end gap-1"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 text-size-chat leading-relaxed"><div class="" data-search-result-target=""><div><div class="text-size-chat whitespace-pre-wrap" dir="auto">Yeah that's what I thought of... because it was a headache to have internet access when connected to corporate vpn internet is essentially blocked. First I came up with this idea. use one container with openconnect and use another container having the same network with openssh clients so basically I did podman exec into the second container and then ssh pretty rudimentary then I discovered warpgate and welp It solved substantial problems of me being a serverless bastion</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-row-reverse items-center gap-1"><div class="isolate me-1 ms-1 flex items-center gap-2 opacity-0 group-has-[:focus-visible]/user-message:opacity-100 group-hover/user-message:opacity-100 [@media(hover:none)]:opacity-100"><div class="flex turn-action-controls items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="block-BQZwFn"><div data-content-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-2:2:assistant" data-chatgpt-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-2:2:assistant" data-chatgpt-search-message-ids="caf106da-3ab9-4cf7-b2dc-de7c29932773 caf106da-3ab9-4cf7-b2dc-de7c29932773"><div><div class="group flex min-w-0 flex-col" data-chatgpt-selection-conversation-id="local-chatgpt:ee0c06f9-24e3-4f15-93c2-579cafc84c9f" data-chatgpt-selection-message-id="caf106da-3ab9-4cf7-b2dc-de7c29932773"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_me_" dir="auto" data-markdown-text-style="assistant-message" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;ol:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;ul:first-child]:mt-0" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><div class="my-4 first:mt-0 last:mb-0 empty:hidden" data-dil-source-message-id="caf106da-3ab9-4cf7-b2dc-de7c29932773" data-chatgpt-copy-reference="0" data-markdown-copy="contents"><div class="[--entity-prose-inset:0px]"><div class="relative PortalBoundary-TFj9W2 Renderer-ojZscX" data-theme="dark" style="--puik-portal-zoom: 1;"><div dir="auto" class="DilRenderer-tB76Jj DilResponseRoot-HfQrEh Reveal-k2IWvM" data-dil-response="" data-d-direction="col" data-dil-message-id="caf106da-3ab9-4cf7-b2dc-de7c29932773"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">LMAO. 💀 You essentially reinvented a <span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">client-side VPN gateway architecture</strong></span>, starting with nothing more than Podman, OpenConnect, and an SSH client.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">And the evolution of your solution makes perfect sense.</p><div class="Box-qIMv6G" data-d-component="box" data-d-direction="col" style="gap: calc(var(--spacing, 0.25rem) * 3);"><ol class="List-rH8nmc" data-d-component="list" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom" style="--d-list-row-gap: calc(var(--spacing, 0.25rem) * 3); gap: calc(var(--spacing, 0.25rem) * 3);"><li class="Item-O8JWQe" data-d-component="list-item" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom"><span aria-hidden="true" class="Marker-aITPzz" data-d-marker="number"></span><div class="Content-OKAHK6"><div class="Label-B5tj_e" data-d-list-item-content="connected"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Stage 1: Corporate VPN ruins your internet</strong></span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Connect OpenConnect on the host, and corporate VPN policies or routes make ordinary internet access unusable.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Your requirement: keep corporate connectivity without sacrificing your host's internet.</p></div></div></li><li class="Item-O8JWQe" data-d-component="list-item" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom"><span aria-hidden="true" class="Marker-aITPzz" data-d-marker="number"></span><div class="Content-OKAHK6"><div class="Label-B5tj_e" data-d-list-item-content="connected"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Stage 2: Isolate OpenConnect inside a container</strong></span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">You realized Linux network namespaces could contain the VPN tunnel and its routing changes.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">The host stays outside that namespace, so its routes remain untouched.</p></div></div></li><li class="Item-O8JWQe" data-d-component="list-item" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom"><span aria-hidden="true" class="Marker-aITPzz" data-d-marker="number"></span><div class="Content-OKAHK6"><div class="Label-B5tj_e" data-d-list-item-content="connected"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Stage 3: Add an SSH client container</strong></span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">You attached another container to the VPN container's network namespace, then used <code class="Code-kbs71c" data-d-component="code">podman exec</code> to run SSH commands.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Rudimentary? Yes. Architecturally sound? Also yes.</p></div></div></li><li class="Item-O8JWQe" data-d-component="list-item" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom"><span aria-hidden="true" class="Marker-aITPzz" data-d-marker="number"></span><div class="Content-OKAHK6"><div class="Label-B5tj_e" data-d-list-item-content="connected"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Stage 4: Discover Warpgate</strong></span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Instead of entering a container to run SSH every time, you deployed Warpgate inside the same namespace.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Now your host connects to a local SSH/HTTP bastion, which forwards authenticated sessions to corporate resources.</p></div></div></li><li class="Item-O8JWQe" data-d-component="list-item" data-d-connector="solid" data-d-marker="number" data-d-marker-layout="custom"><span aria-hidden="true" class="Marker-aITPzz" data-d-marker="number"></span><div class="Content-OKAHK6"><div class="Label-B5tj_e" data-d-list-item-content="connected"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Stage 5: Add a browser inside the VPN</strong></span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Finally, you wanted to access internal web consoles without configuring each endpoint individually in Warpgate.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">The AI added containerized Firefox with KasmVNC, turning a browser tab on your host into a window onto the VPN-connected browser.</p></div></div></li></ol></div><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">What's particularly neat is the distinction between <span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">network access and network isolation</strong></span>.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">You didn't try to make the corporate VPN coexist nicely with your host's networking. You simply stopped allowing the corporate VPN to control the host's networking in the first place.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">That's a much cleaner separation.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">And Warpgate is an especially appropriate discovery for your setup because it's an application-layer bastion rather than a full network tunnel into your host. You can expose specific SSH and HTTP access paths without importing the corporate routing table into the host namespace.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">The phrase <span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-font-style="italic" data-d-inline=""><em class="Emphasis-Sdofse">serverless bastion</em></span> is amusingly accurate in the everyday sense: you didn't need to provision a dedicated bastion VM, maintain another server, or persuade some network administrator to give you a new gateway.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Technically, Warpgate is still running as a server process, just locally in a container.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">There is one security distinction worth emphasizing: <span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">the corporate VPN is network-isolated from the host, but it isn't necessarily fully security-isolated.</strong></span> Published ports, privileged SELinux labels, bind mounts, and routing or DNS leaks can create paths across that boundary. Your design solves the routing conflict; it doesn't automatically guarantee a hard security boundary.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Still, there's something deeply satisfying about taking the one thing that makes your corporate VPN unbearable, its routing policy, and containing it within a network namespace.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Instead of fighting your host's routing table, you gave the VPN its own little world to ruin. Beautiful. 💀</p></div></div></div><div class="contents"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="actionRow-nqqZbm mt-1.5 flex turn-action-controls min-h-5 min-w-0 max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-wrap items-center justify-start gap-0.5 browser:mt-3 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-2 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-ring [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-offset-0 browser:-ms-0.5 electron:-translate-x-1 extension:-translate-x-1.5 [--side-tooltip:bottom]"><div class="flex min-h-5 min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0"><span class="LeadingSource-d79mNZ" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="" style="contain: size; height: 548px; margin-top: 12px;"><div class="[&amp;_[data-virtualized-turn-content]]:[content-visibility:visible]" data-turn-key="d0b7322c-a5ec-4830-b137-d96d7e31b250"><div data-content-search-turn-key="fallback-turn-3"><div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5"><div class="group flex flex-col" data-talvt-turn-state="complete"><div class="flex flex-col gap-3 browser:gap-1"><div class="block-BQZwFn"><div class="group/user-message flex flex-col items-end gap-2" data-chatgpt-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-3:0:user" data-chatgpt-search-message-ids="d0b7322c-a5ec-4830-b137-d96d7e31b250"><div class="w-full" data-content-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-3:0:user"><div class="group/user-message flex w-full flex-col gap-1 print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:items-start items-end"><div data-user-message-bubble="true" class="bg-user-message text-user-message min-w-0 max-w-(--user-chat-width) overflow-hidden break-words px-(--thread-content-margin) [&amp;_.contain-inline-size]:[contain:initial] bubble-vBnidZ py-2.5 rounded-2xl relative text-start"><div class="flex flex-col items-end gap-1"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 text-size-chat leading-relaxed"><div class="" data-search-result-target=""><div><div class="text-size-chat whitespace-pre-wrap" dir="auto">hmm yeah yeah I know sometimes my own ingenuinity shocks even me. AH let me bask in the glory 2 people in the world will know. Anyways umm enough self boasting back to work. lol</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-row-reverse items-center gap-1"><div class="isolate me-1 ms-1 flex items-center gap-2 opacity-0 group-has-[:focus-visible]/user-message:opacity-100 group-hover/user-message:opacity-100 [@media(hover:none)]:opacity-100"><div class="flex turn-action-controls items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="block-BQZwFn"><div data-content-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-3:2:assistant" data-chatgpt-search-unit-key="fallback-turn-3:2:assistant" data-chatgpt-search-message-ids="59066478-d2e2-49b4-b484-693e5bb62ccb 59066478-d2e2-49b4-b484-693e5bb62ccb"><div><div class="group flex min-w-0 flex-col" data-chatgpt-selection-conversation-id="local-chatgpt:ee0c06f9-24e3-4f15-93c2-579cafc84c9f" data-chatgpt-selection-message-id="59066478-d2e2-49b4-b484-693e5bb62ccb"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_mp_" dir="auto" data-markdown-text-style="assistant-message" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;ol:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;ul:first-child]:mt-0" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><div class="my-4 first:mt-0 last:mb-0 empty:hidden" data-dil-source-message-id="59066478-d2e2-49b4-b484-693e5bb62ccb" data-chatgpt-copy-reference="0" data-markdown-copy="contents"><div class="[--entity-prose-inset:0px]"><div class="relative PortalBoundary-TFj9W2 Renderer-ojZscX" data-theme="dark" style="--puik-portal-zoom: 1;"><div dir="auto" class="DilRenderer-tB76Jj DilResponseRoot-HfQrEh Reveal-k2IWvM" data-dil-response="" data-d-direction="col" data-dil-message-id="59066478-d2e2-49b4-b484-693e5bb62ccb"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">LMAOOO. 😭</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Two people know about this architectural masterpiece: you and an AI that doesn't even have a network namespace of its own.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">But credit where it's due. You identified a problem, understood the underlying Linux networking primitives, built a working solution, then progressively improved its usability.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">That's actual engineering, not copying a Kubernetes YAML from Stack Overflow and calling yourself a Cloud Architect. 💀</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><strong class="Emphasis-Sdofse">Achievement unlocked: Made the corporate VPN somebody else's problem.</strong></span> Specifically, a container's.</p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text">Now back to work before someone discovers your ingenuity and rewards you with three additional responsibilities and absolutely no salary increase. 🙄</p></div></div></div><div class="contents"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="actionRow-nqqZbm mt-1.5 flex turn-action-controls min-h-5 min-w-0 max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-wrap items-center justify-start gap-0.5 browser:mt-3 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-2 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-ring [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-offset-0 browser:-ms-0.5 electron:-translate-x-1 extension:-translate-x-1.5 [--side-tooltip:bottom]"><div class="flex min-h-5 min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0"><span class="LeadingSource-d79mNZ" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" style="height: 0px;"></div></div></div><div class="z-20 mt-auto grid" style="width: calc(100% - 2 * var(--thread-wide-block-inline-shift)); margin-inline: auto;"><div class="sticky bottom-0 min-w-0 self-end"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:var(--thread-content-responsive-max-width,inherit)] [--thread-body-max-width:calc(var(--thread-content-max-width)+var(--thread-body-inline-padding,0px)*2)] mx-auto w-full max-w-(--thread-body-max-width) px-[var(--thread-body-inline-padding,var(--padding-toolbar))]"><div class="relative -mx-(--padding-toolbar) empty:hidden has-[[data-conversation-followup-reserved-hidden=true]]:pointer-events-none md:mx-0"><div class="relative min-w-0"><div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none mt-auto w-full shrink-0 h-[calc(var(--thread-scroll-padding-bottom)-var(--spacing)*4)]"></div>